  "headline": "City of Nawabs",
  "short_description": "Lucknow is celebrated for Awadhi cuisine, Nawabi-era architecture and refined Ganga-Jamuni tehzeeb (composite culture).",
  "about": "The former capital of the Nawabs of Awadh, Lucknow is known for its grand imambaras, intricate chikankari embroidery and some of India's finest kebabs.\n\nLocated on the banks of the Gomti river in central Uttar Pradesh.\n\nRenowned for Urdu poetry, classical Kathak dance, chikankari embroidery and elaborate courtesy (tehzeeb).\n\nA historic centre of Shia Islam in India alongside a large Hindu population.",
  "history": "Rose to prominence under the Nawabs of Awadh in the 18th century and was a key site during the 1857 uprising, notably at the Residency.",
  "history_verified": false,
  "transportation": "- Chaudhary Charan Singh International Airport (airport)\n- Lucknow Charbagh Railway Station (railway)\n- Alambagh Bus Station (bus terminal)",
  "travel_info": "Languages: Hindi, Urdu, English\nBudget: mid range",
  "best_time_text": "October to March",
  "ideal_duration_text": "2 days",
